U2D2 port: /dev/serial/by-id/usb-FTDI_USB__-__Serial_Converter_FTAOAFC5-if00-port0
           (/dev/serial/by-id -> /dev/ttyUSB0)
WHOLE-BODY TORQUE (flight topology). The arm is LIVE on activation and MOVES TO HOME:
[0, 40, 40, 0] deg (inverted — the EE folds reached-out under the mount).
BASELINE (SAFETY): this controller's own PD+ holds the arm. DIRECT, from the drone
ground station's whole-body button: the flight node's coupled law owns it and this
side adds nothing. Whoever streams owns the arm; there is no mode to set here.
TORQUE MODE: EEPROM limits do NOT bind (Mode 16) — the controller's software
limits are the only position guard, and a stopped controller = LIMP ARM.
CLEAR THE WORKSPACE — starting now.

============================================================================
 Whole-body arm side (flight topology) -- arm at /uav_0/fsc_open_manipulator
 controller: external_torque_controller. Baseline mode: its own PD+ holds the
             arm. Whole-body DIRECT: pure pass-through of the coupled law's
             torques from /uav_0/fsc_autopilot_ros2. The switch is the stream
             itself; SAFETY/DIRECT is the drone ground station's button.
 command mode: pwm
 The flight node reads the arm reference at
   /uav_0/fsc_open_manipulator/external_torque_controller/smoothed_reference_joint_trajectory
 and streams torques to
   /uav_0/fsc_open_manipulator/external_torque_controller/joint_torque_command
 -> "THE EXTERNAL LAW NOW OWNS THE ARM" in the log = whole-body DIRECT.
    "THE LOCAL PD+ HOLD NOW OWNS THE ARM" = baseline mode, which is also what
    you get if the flight stack is down or in the wrong namespace.

 GROUND STATION — separate terminal (laptop); no flag needed:
   scripts/indoor_exp/start_ground_station_inverted.sh /uav_0/fsc_open_manipulator

 Ctrl-C here stops the arm but NOT the station or the flight stack.
 To take the arm side down from any terminal:
   scripts/indoor_exp/stop_open_manipulator_stack.sh
